## Context
Audit after the 0116 merge surfaced 11 small doc/comment issues — none
breaking, all worth a single cleanup pass. Two themes: stale or thin
doc comments on Go types and functions, and error messages that say
what's wrong but not what to do.

## Doc-comment thinness / staleness
1. `Erg.BlockedBys` field comment says values are stored "verbatim" but
   `parseHeaderLine` trims them — erg.go:24.
2. `Erg` struct doc "schema-literal projection" is terse; doesn't
   state the lenient-parse invariant — erg.go:15.
3. `FilenameID` returns empty-string for non-numeric stems (callers in
   close/archive/check guard, but the contract is unstated) — erg.go:106.
4. `Filename()` doc only restates signature; no non-empty invariant
   stated — erg.go:101.
5. `parseHeaderLine` doc one-liner; omits `Key :` (space-before-colon)
   whitespace handling — erg.go:123.
6. `v1HeaderKeys` comment references "validate.go data (which 0116
   commit 4 removes anyway)" — stale historical reference — erg.go:161.
7. `updateURL` const lacks doc explaining it's the ERG_UPDATE_URL
   default — update.go:13.

## Error-message helpfulness (what's wrong AND what to do)
8. Title/Created/Author "missing or empty required header" errors
   don't say what to do (add the header to the preamble) — validate.go:24-31.
9. Generic unknown-header error lacks a "remove or run `erg migrate`"
   hint; Status/Tags paths do — validate.go:46.
10. Rule-3a "unknown Tag value '%s' (not in v1 closed set)" doesn't
    list the closed set — validate.go:58.

## Rule-numbering coherence
11. `validateErg` comments use rule numbers 1, 2, 3, 3a, 4, 5, 6, 7,
    8, 10, 11 (validate.go:18-122). `helpValidate` uses 1-13. Mapping
    a user-visible error to a documented rule is harder than it should
    be. Reconcile the numbering — either renumber the code comments
    to match helpValidate, or renumber helpValidate. Recommendation:
    renumber code comments to match user-visible numbering.

## Actions
1. Apply each fix above; one commit per logical group is fine, or one
   sweep commit if minor.
2. Verify `make test` passes (these are docs/strings; should be a
   no-op for tests except where tests assert on error messages).
3. Spec/help-text updates: any change to user-visible error wording
   means updating shell-test fixtures in `tests/test_validate.sh`.

## Out of scope
- Defer-to-0117 items (rule-numbering will move under 0117 too —
  coordinate; if 0117 is imminent, fold this ticket's rule-numbering
  item into 0117 instead).

## Exit criteria
- All 11 items addressed.
- `make test` passes.
- No user-visible error wording regresses (or shell fixtures updated
  to match).
